      "committer": {
        "name": "GitHub",
        "email": "noreply@github.com",
        "date": "2026-09-10T08:13:36Z"
      },
      "message": "Don't let malformed set_parameters requests crash the node (#3256)\n\nThe set_parameters and set_parameters_atomically service handlers only\ncaught ParameterNotDeclaredException. A request carrying a parameter with\nan empty name (InvalidParametersException) or an unknown value type\n(UnknownTypeError, thrown by Parameter::from_parameter_msg) let the\nexception escape the service callback, unwind through the executor's\nspin(), and terminate the node -- an unauthenticated remote DoS on any\nnode exposing the default parameter services.\n\nBroaden both handlers to catch std::exception and return an unsuccessful\nSetParametersResult instead. In the atomic handler, move the\nfrom_parameter_msg conversion inside the try so an unknown type raised\nduring conversion is handled too.\n\nAdds regression tests covering empty name (typed client) and unknown\ntype (raw client) for both services.\n\nSigned-off-by: Bas Zalmstra <4995967+baszalmstra@users.noreply.github.com>\nSigned-off-by: Alejandro Hernandez Cordero <ahcorde@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Alejandro Hernandez Cordero <ahcorde@gmail.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "2596cf59e98f88925c3ead1f9ff43c561447bf0c",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ros2/rclcpp/git/trees/2596cf59e98f88925c3ead1f9ff43c561447bf0c"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ros2/rclcpp/git/commits/2e5a8b9ea68d03ebd24627a91abc8f105fe81661",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqomawCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1JUQALFdSaJXlknfkoD2N++niT1x\nK4I5janLuY0frthbrQEldOX9lWSCOL2X4XfTjjJ1D2tziClRw4VOm4ZaSrODCEU0\nnHKeXS+TgEyQm25kxRm9ki5b4YDzv9mzAC3LfYxFOuQyZyrmSv8fzr9Vz8gvduCW\nxZhDqNrG5DmfmQ3QF1qjTbl2LrBDyctnXQBhh0c+3iWhaZ7Wj9RWVondT5P3ugUu\nodejEQwfslEBcfEvhazZQ8SU08MepdgMDZ3HA6q4LKTcoQ8XTf759uyxVbu6POXh\nX9k69nR09u1MllE6fJx/jpF6z1ydAKcKMjVuiXSsJuKqlNXaIY/zHZkYVSonqs2b\nMAo5IOOzNSdVWmKZppiA1bvAejvXCInipOPX39LsfyQ5slRHiA5o7g59niIlKxZU\n3Urefgf2qDLkhIDasBdvRTggpb1HYF+ArR5NN5gD/aYEw+ADRsK36XFrlHpxcQns\nAP+RyxvHkGh4GsKi/iuWrNWHqUhCPiC5g/LUqUmNa1FmD4IzaE918rMybck+HLyX\nPeUuTil2GzhxLuBmna594j1Uw2egiNWxfUueSTXbiS6Ld+OZ9o/qbJagDgOt04RF\nk/U5tTxrDKmLHmVqTaBSOpbSbuFOs5RJXis0l1MskwXfdz9HwIn979lBUTPeMx90\n59p/21bWlShrJZyZBQ03\n=2u2d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 2596cf59e98f88925c3ead1f9ff43c561447bf0c\nparent c36e550282d41fc151872470b6958507784baa4c\nauthor Bas Zalmstra <4995967+baszalmstra@users.noreply.github.com> 1789028016 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789028016 +0200\n\nDon't let malformed set_parameters requests crash the node (#3256)\n\nThe set_parameters and set_parameters_atomically service handlers only\ncaught ParameterNotDeclaredException. A request carrying a parameter with\nan empty name (InvalidParametersException) or an unknown value type\n(UnknownTypeError, thrown by Parameter::from_parameter_msg) let the\nexception escape the service callback, unwind through the executor's\nspin(), and terminate the node -- an unauthenticated remote DoS on any\nnode exposing the default parameter services.\n\nBroaden both handlers to catch std::exception and return an unsuccessful\nSetParametersResult instead. In the atomic handler, move the\nfrom_parameter_msg conversion inside the try so an unknown type raised\nduring conversion is handled too.\n\nAdds regression tests covering empty name (typed client) and unknown\ntype (raw client) for both services.\n\nSigned-off-by: Bas Zalmstra <4995967+baszalmstra@users.noreply.github.com>\nSigned-off-by: Alejandro Hernandez Cordero <ahcorde@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Alejandro Hernandez Cordero <ahcorde@gmail.com>",
